  "result": "The six-question quiz on O4 is ready. It is `quizzes/0002.json`, and its key is `keys/0002.json`.\n\n- **Topic:** who owns the control flow, the model or our code, and when a fixed workflow is the better choice.\n- **Questions:** five multiple-choice, one short answer and one numeric. All use makerspace-assistant examples, and one is a cost comparison tied to your budget.\n- **Order:** the quiz starts with the definition, moves to classifying designs, then to choosing between workflow and agent for real tasks.\n- **Timing:** this quiz is ahead of the lessons. There is no O4 lesson yet, so I wrote it as a check of the objective itself. It draws on Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\" distinction, which I wrote from memory and did not look up in this session. I can write a lesson on O4 whenever you want one.\n- **Misconception ids:** the distractors use M7 to M9, which are new. I didn't reuse M1 to M6 because they already mean other things.\n\nI didn't write `NOTES.md` or a learning record, since nothing has been graded yet.\n\nI have a question for you: do you want to take the quiz here in the chat, or have a short O4 lesson first?",
